Package: ai-revive
Architecture: all
Depends: tmux (>= 3.0), jq, bash (>= 4.4), procps, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: byobu
Suggests: inotify-tools
Description: save and restore tmux/byobu workspaces across reboots
 ai-revive snapshots every tmux session, window, pane, working directory
 and layout, and brings them back after a reboot, including the program
 that was running in each pane. Claude Code conversations are resumed by
 session id, ssh connections are re-established with their original
 command line, and any other program can be whitelisted.
 .
 It works as a plain tmux plugin (TPM compatible) and integrates with
 byobu: `ai-revive enable` wires it into the user's byobu configuration,
 installs tmux hooks that save on every layout change and a systemd user
 timer for periodic snapshots, and restores the workspace automatically
 when byobu starts after a reboot.
